.TH GIT-WHEN 1 "September 2026" "git when" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-when \- find when a term appeared, went away, or changed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git when
.RI [ --all ]
.RI [ --plain ]
.RI [ changed | added | removed | matching ]
.I TERM
.RI [ PATH ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git when
searches commit history for changes involving
.IR TERM .
With no verb, it finds commits containing a changed line that matches the
regular expression
.IR TERM .
.TP
.BI changed " TERM"
Find commits where the number of occurrences of the fixed string
.I TERM
changed.
.TP
.BI added " TERM"
Find commits where the number of occurrences of the fixed string
.I TERM
increased in at least one file.
.TP
.BI removed " TERM"
Find commits where the number of occurrences of the fixed string
.I TERM
decreased in at least one file.
.TP
.BI matching " TERM"
Explicit form of the default regular-expression search.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --all
Search every ref instead of only the history reachable from HEAD.
.TP
.B --plain
Print one line per commit instead of opening the interactive picker.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help.
.TP
.B --
End option parsing. Remaining arguments limit the search to those paths.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git when 'old_name'
Find commits with changed lines matching
.BR old_name .
.TP
.B git when added 'new_name' -- src/
Find commits that added occurrences of
.B new_name
under
.BR src/ .
